Investigated permission discrepancy between dashboard and admin access

That's actually the system working correctly — not a bug. Here's why:

/dashboard only requires the auth middleware → any logged-in user gets in.
/admin requires auth plus role:admin → only accounts where role = 'admin' in the 
database get in. Everyone else gets a 403.

When you registered, AuthController::register() sets 'role' => 'user' by default for 
every new signup. So unless you manually promoted your account to admin, you're supposed 
to be blocked from /admin.

To become admin, run this once:

bash
php artisan tinker
php
$u = App\Models\User::where('email', 'your@email.com')->first();
$u->role = 'admin';
$u->save();

Then log out and log back in (or just refresh /dashboard) —
 you should now see the "Go to Admin Page" button, and visiting /admin should load 
 the page instead of showing a 403.

Quick check — when you visit /admin directly right now, do you see a 403 Forbidden page, or
 something else (blank page, redirect, error)?
 That'll confirm whether it's just the expected role restriction, or a different problem.